/*
CSS BOX MODEL – DEFAULT vs ALTERNATE

The CSS box model controls how the browser calculates an element’s size 
using content, padding, border, and margin.

==================== CSS BOX MODEL (WITH DIAGRAM) ====================

Example used in BOTH models:
width  = 200px
padding = 20px
border  = 5px


--------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFAULT BOX MODEL (content-box)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

- This is the browser’s default behavior.
- The given width and height apply ONLY to the content.
- Padding and border are added outside the width and height.
- Adding padding or border increases the total size of the element,
  which can cause layout shifts.

Diagram (values applied):

Total Width = 250px

+---------------------------------------------------+
|                Border (5px)                       |
|   +-------------------------------------------+   |
|   |             Padding (20px)                |   |
|   |   +-----------------------------------+   |   |
|   |   |     Content = 200px width          |   |   |
|   |   +-----------------------------------+   |   |
|   +-------------------------------------------+   |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Calculation:
200px (content)
+ 40px (padding left + right)
+ 10px (border left + right)
--------------------------------
= 250px TOTAL WIDTH


--------------------------------------------------------------------
ALTERNATE BOX MODEL (border-box)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
- Enabled using box-sizing: border-box.
- The given width and height include content, padding, and border.
- The total element size stays fixed.
- The content area shrinks automatically when padding or border is added.
- Makes layouts predictable and easier to manage, especially in responsive designs.

Diagram (values applied):

Total Width = 200px (FIXED)

+-----------------------------------------------+
|               Border (5px)                    |
|   +---------------------------------------+   |
|   |           Padding (20px)              |   |
|   |   +-----------------------------+     |   |
|   |   |   Content (auto adjusted)   |     |   |
|   |   +-----------------------------+     |   |
|   +---------------------------------------+   |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Calculation:
Total width = 200px
Padding + border fit INSIDE
Content adjusts automatically


--------------------------------------------------------------------
MEMORY TIP
--------------------------------------------------------------------

content-box → width = content only (box grows)
border-box  → width = whole box (box stays same)


--------------------------------------------------------------------
BEST PRACTICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------

* {
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

- Prevents layout breaking
- Predictable sizing
- Used in modern CSS
*/
